      "summaries": {
        "en": "Ghostty is a cross-platform terminal emulator designed for speed and rich features, leveraging GPU acceleration and native UI to deliver a responsive experience. Its key technical insight is using Zig for performance and safety, with a renderer that offloads work to the GPU, reducing latency. You can use it as a daily driver on macOS, Linux, or Windows, or extend it via its configuration system for custom workflows. Ideal for developers seeking a modern, fast terminal without sacrificing platform integration.",
        "zh": "Ghostty 是一款跨平台终端模拟器，主打快速、功能丰富，通过 GPU 加速和原生 UI 实现流畅体验。其技术亮点在于使用 Zig 语言开发，兼顾性能与安全性，渲染引擎将工作负载卸载到 GPU，显著降低延迟。你可以在 macOS、Linux 或 Windows 上将其作为日常终端使用，或通过配置文件自定义快捷键、主题等，适配个人工作流。适合追求现代、快速且与系统深度集成的开发者，无需牺牲平台原生体验即可获得高效终端工具。",
        "es": "Ghostty is a cross-platform terminal emulator designed for speed and rich features, leveraging GPU acceleration and native UI to deliver a responsive experience. Its key technical insight is using Zig for performance and safety, with a renderer that offloads work to the GPU, reducing latency. You can use it as a daily driver on macOS, Linux, or Windows, or extend it via its configuration system for custom workflows. Ideal for developers seeking a modern, fast terminal without sacrificing platform integration.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "ghostty gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Ghostty is a cross-platform terminal emulator designed for speed and rich features, leveraging GPU acceleration and native UI to deliver a responsive experience. Its key technical insight is using Zig for performance and safety, with a renderer that offloads work to the GPU, reducing latency. You can use it as a daily driver on macOS, Linux, or Windows, or extend it via its configuration system for custom workflows. Ideal for developers seeking a modern, fast terminal without sacrificing platform integration.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/ghostty-org/ghostty for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
