      "summaries": {
        "en": "Open Source CS is a curated, self-taught computer science curriculum based on top university courses. It solves the problem of fragmented online learning by providing a structured path covering core CS topics like algorithms, systems, and theory. The curriculum uses free, high-quality materials from MIT, Stanford, and others, emphasizing project-based learning. You can follow the suggested order or pick courses to fill knowledge gaps, making it ideal for self-learners seeking a rigorous, cost-free CS education.",
        "zh": "Open Source CS 是一个精心策划的计算机科学自学课程体系，旨在解决在线学习资源碎片化的问题。它借鉴了麻省理工、斯坦福等顶尖大学的公开课程，按逻辑顺序组织核心科目，如算法、系统与理论，强调项目驱动的学习方式。该课程完全免费，适合希望系统性掌握CS知识、但缺乏传统教育背景的自学者。你可以按推荐路径循序渐进，或选择特定课程弥补知识短板，从而获得扎实的计算机科学基础。",
        "es": "Open Source CS is a curated, self-taught computer science curriculum based on top university courses. It solves the problem of fragmented online learning by providing a structured path covering core CS topics like algorithms, systems, and theory. The curriculum uses free, high-quality materials from MIT, Stanford, and others, emphasizing project-based learning. You can follow the suggested order or pick courses to fill knowledge gaps, making it ideal for self-learners seeking a rigorous, cost-free CS education.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "open-source-cs stands out for computer-science in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "Open Source CS is a curated, self-taught computer science curriculum based on top university courses. It solves the problem of fragmented online learning by providing a structured path covering core CS topics like algorithms, systems, and theory. The curriculum uses free, high-quality materials from MIT, Stanford, and others, emphasizing project-based learning. You can follow the suggested order or pick courses to fill knowledge gaps, making it ideal for self-learners seeking a rigorous, cost-free CS education.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/ForrestKnight/open-source-cs for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
      },
