      "summaries": {
        "en": "Skills is an SDK for building AI agents that can browse the web using Claude. It provides a structured way to define tools and actions, enabling agents to navigate pages, extract data, and fill forms. The key technical insight is its modular design, allowing developers to compose complex browsing behaviors from simple, reusable skills. You can use it to automate web research, testing, or data collection tasks by defining custom skills in JavaScript.",
        "zh": "Skills 是一个基于Claude模型的AI智能体SDK，支持网页浏览能力。其核心亮点是模块化设计，通过结构化工具和动作定义，使智能体可导航页面、提取数据、填写表单。开发者能用JavaScript定义自定义技能，将简单可复用的技能组合成复杂浏览行为，用于自动化网页研究、测试或数据收集等任务。该SDK降低了构建实用网页智能体的门槛，适合需要自动化浏览器交互的场景。",
        "es": "Skills is an SDK for building AI agents that can browse the web using Claude. It provides a structured way to define tools and actions, enabling agents to navigate pages, extract data, and fill forms. The key technical insight is its modular design, allowing developers to compose complex browsing behaviors from simple, reusable skills. You can use it to automate web research, testing, or data collection tasks by defining custom skills in JavaScript.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "skills gives teams a dependable path to production-ready AI tooling.",
          "what": "Skills is an SDK for building AI agents that can browse the web using Claude. It provides a structured way to define tools and actions, enabling agents to navigate pages, extract data, and fill forms. The key technical insight is its modular design, allowing developers to compose complex browsing behaviors from simple, reusable skills. You can use it to automate web research, testing, or data collection tasks by defining custom skills in JavaScript.",
          "how": "Review https://github.com/browserbase/skills for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
